 "title": "Who to talk to at a networking event",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "This video provides tips on who to approach at a networking event and who to skip. The creator explains how to identify approachable people and start low-pressure conversations.",
 "key_points": [
  "Do not interrupt someone who is busy taking a food photo or on their phone.",
  "Do not approach someone who looks as confused as you are.",
  "Instead of asking 'What do you do?', try asking 'What are you more excited about, the conference or the food?'.",
  "Do not stop people who are walking in the opposite direction.",
  "Approach someone who is standing alone and not rushing, and ask how the food is or say hi.",
  "You do not need a long conversation; a solid five-minute high-energy conversation where you are curious about them beats everything."
 ],
 "content": "Who to talk to at a networking event (and who to skip) Do not interrupt her, the food photo comes first He looks as confused as you are, don't approach him Go stand behind him, skip the w-what do you do Try this: What are you more excited about, the conference or the food? She's going in the opposite direction, don't make people stop for you She's standing alone, not rushing, ask her how the food is and say hi Here's exactly where most people mess up You think you need to have a long amazing conversation You don't A solid five-minute high-energy conversation where you're curious about them beats everything Vibe is good, you guys match, connect, and go forward Follow to get social in situations that builds your confidence!",
